<task id="072" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>`npm run lint` points at a directory that does not exist and no workflow calls it — CI passes because lint never runs</title>
    <phase>5 Remediation — verification</phase>
    <gate>blocked — requires 069 (adds to the same gate)</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies a CI workflow and will change `.ts`/`.tsx` files to satisfy newly-running rules. Tags include ci-cd.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Mechanical: point the script at the real directories, fix what it reports, wire it in. The reference (the PCF ESLint jobs) already exists.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>C</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Disjoint from 071's test files and 073's Node config — but shares the workflow with 069/070, so sequence after those.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>069</deps>
    <tags>ci-cd, devops, typescript, frontend</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-5 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>`package.json:13` runs `eslint src` in a package that has no `src/` directory, and no workflow invokes it. Point it at the real source, fix what it finds, and wire it into the gate.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer.</role>

  <goal>Lint runs over the office-addins source on every PR and can fail the build.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Found 2026-09-21 by the Fable verification review (`notes/fable-review-2026-09-21.md` §8).

      `src/client/office-addins/package.json:13` is `eslint src`. There is no `src/` directory in that
      package — the sources live under `shared/`, `word/` and `outlook/`. Running it produces
      *"No files matching the pattern src"*.

      No workflow calls it. The repo's ESLint jobs run in `src/client/pcf`
      (`ci-tier2-advisory.yml:183-194`, `sdap-ci.yml:404-427`), not here.

      **CI passes because lint never runs, not because lint passes.** Nobody knows how many violations exist
      in this package, because the script has never successfully executed against it.

      Expect the first real run to report a backlog. That backlog is the finding; sizing it is part of this
      task.
    </background>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="this task">Do NOT weaken rules to get a green run. If the backlog is large, fix it or scope the initial gate to a rule subset with the remainder tracked explicitly — silently disabling rules recreates the "control exists but decides nothing" pattern this whole wave is fixing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">`ci-tier2-advisory.yml` and the other tiered workflows are FROZEN. Wire lint into `office-addins-tests.yml`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="this task">Apply task 069's lesson: prove the new lint job can fail, on CI, by seeding a violation.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run lint` executes against the real source directories and reports a result. Record the raw violation count from the FIRST successful run — that number is the finding.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The violation backlog is driven to zero, OR the initial gate is scoped to a stated rule subset with the remainder recorded in the task note as named, counted follow-up. State which, and why.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Lint runs in `office-addins-tests.yml` on every PR touching the package.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">PROVEN ON CI IN BOTH DIRECTIONS: seed a lint violation, show the job red; remove it, show green. Record both run URLs.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No ESLint rule is disabled or downgraded to achieve green without an explicit one-line justification per rule in the task note.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`actionlint` passes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the first real lint run reports a backlog large enough that fixing it would dominate this task (say, hundreds of violations), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 with the counts by rule and the options — do not silently disable rules, and do not silently leave lint unwired.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>`npm install` first (this desktop's install is stale — see 073).</step>
    <step>Point the script at the real directories; run it; record the raw backlog by rule.</step>
    <step>Decide: fix all, or gate a subset with the remainder named. Record the reasoning.</step>
    <step>Wire it into `office-addins-tests.yml`.</step>
    <step>Prove red and green on CI; record both run URLs.</step>
    <step>Write `notes/072-lint.md` with the backlog table. Update TASK-INDEX.md: 072 → ✅.</step>
  </steps>

  <relevant-files>
    <file role="edit">src/client/office-addins/package.json</file>
    <file role="edit">.github/workflows/office-addins-tests.yml</file>
    <file role="new">projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/072-lint.md</file>
  </relevant-files>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>docs/procedures/testing-and-code-quality.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/CODING-STANDARDS.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/fable-review-2026-09-21.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <outputs>
    <file>src/client/office-addins/package.json</file>
    <file>projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/072-lint.md</file>
  </outputs>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load all files in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt; before starting. Task 069 must be ✅ first — same workflow file.</protocol>
  </execution>

  <status-note date="2026-09-28">
    COMPLETED. Full record: notes/072-lint.md.

    THE FINDING (the number nobody had): the first successful lint run reported 32
    violations -- 4 errors, 28 warnings -- across 17 of 125 files. 13
    no-empty-function, 12 no-unused-vars, 3 react-hooks/exhaustive-deps, 2 no-namespace
    (error), 1 no-case-declarations (error), 1 no-var-requires (error). Not hundreds, so
    the escalation trigger did not fire, and the backlog is driven to ZERO.

    NO RULE DISABLED OR DOWNGRADED. One rule OPTION changed and it is the rule's own:
    no-namespace gains allowDeclarations, because both hits are
    `declare global { namespace Office { ... } }` -- global augmentation CANNOT be
    expressed in ES2015 module syntax, so the rule's advice has no applicable form, and
    the declaration is erased at compile time so no runtime namespace is created.
    Non-declaration namespaces remain errors.

    The 13 empty functions needed no config change because I PROBED rather than assumed:
    ESLint treats a body containing a comment as non-empty, so each became
    `{ /* no-op */ }`. The obvious alternative -- an overrides block for __tests__ --
    would have switched a rule off across a quarter of the package to fix 11 stubs.

    --max-warnings 0 is load-bearing and is now proven so: 28 of 32 were WARNINGS, so
    without it this gate would have gone green over 87% of the backlog.

    TWO INERT SUPPRESSIONS FOUND, both the same class as the defects 069 and 070 fixed:
    (1) DocumentProfileSection.tsx wrapped an eslint-disable-next-line justification onto
    a SECOND // line, so "next line" resolved to the comment and the rule still fired;
    (2) matterTypeLookupService.cache.test.ts disabled no-require-imports while the rule
    that actually fires under typescript-eslint 6 is no-var-requires. Neither was
    discoverable until lint ran once.

    ONE REAL CODE IMPROVEMENT, not a suppression: EntityPicker's allOptions was a bare
    const [] + .push(), a new array identity every render, which made the useCallback
    below it re-create every render -- the memoisation was doing nothing, and that is
    what the rule reported. Now useMemo'd with explicit deps; contents unchanged. The
    other two exhaustive-deps sites are genuine intentional omissions with per-site
    reasons. no-case-declarations in SseClient.ts was a real minor defect (a const
    scoped to the whole switch, so a later cross-branch reference would be a runtime
    ReferenceError).

    CROSS-TASK INTERACTION, caught locally: six unused locals were ALSO counted by tsc's
    noUnusedLocals, so 069's pinned debt fell 74 -> 68. Because that pin is an EQUALITY
    and not a ceiling, CI would have refused the reduction until it was written down --
    the pin working exactly as designed on its first real encounter. Re-baselined to 68
    in the same PR. Production errors remain 0.

    CI PROOFS: green 36459612571 (all four jobs; pin verified in-run at 68), red
    36460853616 (ESLint failure on "1 problem (0 errors, 1 warning)" -> "ESLint found too
    many warnings (maximum: 0)" while the other three jobs stayed GREEN -- clean
    isolation), then revert -> green.

    AN OWN GOAL THAT WOULD HAVE PRODUCED A FALSE PROOF: the first seed was named
    __072_unusedSeed, and .eslintrc sets varsIgnorePattern ^_ , so the leading underscore
    made ESLint ignore it BY DESIGN. Local lint exited 0; had I pushed it, CI would have
    gone green and the record would have claimed a proof that the gate cannot fail.
    Proving the seed locally before pushing is what caught it. The second attempt also
    needed narrowing, because an unused const trips tsc's noUnusedLocals too and would
    have reddened the typecheck job as well, leaving no clean attribution.

    OUT-OF-SCOPE FINDING, deliberately NOT absorbed here and needing a decision:
    SaveFlow.test.tsx contains FIVE it(...) blocks with NO assertions -- they build mocks
    and carry only a comment saying the test would require more work. They PASS, and the
    file is in ci-gated-suites.txt, so the 56-suite gate counts them as coverage. That is
    ADR-038's banned coverage-filler class and vacuous green one level below anything
    069/070/072 addressed. I did NOT delete the now-unused fixtures, because that would
    make the empty tests look tidy while still asserting nothing; they are _-prefixed
    using the rule's own convention, recording the honest state -- pending, not dead.
    Route to /test-diet at 090 or its own task.

    DID NOT CLOSE: lint runs and can fail the workflow run, but does not BLOCK a merge --
    the ruleset requires only Router. Same owner action as 069 and 070.
  </status-note>
</task>
